 "title": "Alberta Voted on a Vote About Leaving Canada. Why?",
 "voice": "am_michael",
 "speed": 1.0,
 "description": "On Monday, October 19, 2026, Alberta held its first-ever vote on separation: not on leaving Canada, but on whether to START the legal process for a binding separation referendum. With more than 1.8 million votes counted, about 75% chose to remain (unofficial; official results Oct 29). We go through how the vote got on the ballot, why many Albertans are angry with Ottawa (oil, taxes, history), the U.S. trade war and '51st state' talk, what each side says now, the nine other questions, and whether a province could even leave. Stick figures, facts only.\n\nDave and Linda are made-up characters. Real people are shown as generic labelled stick figures; statements are attributed as reported.\n\nSources:\nAP via PBS NewsHour, Alberta voters reject independence from Canada in victory for Carney (Oct 20, 2026): https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/alberta-voters-reject-independence-from-canada-in-victory-for-carney\nAl Jazeera, Alberta voters reject separation from Canada, early results show (Oct 20, 2026): https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/20/alberta-voters-reject-separation-from-canada-early-results-show\nAxios, Alberta referendum results: Voters reject push for independence from Canada (Oct 20, 2026): https://www.axios.com/2026/10/20/alberta-canada-referendum-results-remain\nCTV News / CP24 live updates (Oct 20, 2026): https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/10/20/albertans-reject-separation-in-historic-vote-ctv-news-projects-live-updates/\nGlobal News, Albertans mixed on other referendum questions after rejecting separation: https://globalnews.ca/news/12109093/alberta-referendum-separation-other-results/\nWikipedia, 2026 Alberta independence referendum / Alberta separatism (background, petitions, polls): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Alberta_independence_referendum\nElections Qu\u00e9bec, 1995 referendum results: https://www.electionsquebec.qc.ca/en/results-and-statistics/1995-referendum-on-quebecs-accession-to-sovereignty/\n\n#alberta #canada #ref